REGISTERED PREDICTIONS. Printed before anything is measured, and not rewritten afterwards.

  P1  a healthy card holds a clock well clear of its own floor
        predicts  the median SM clock over the scored window is at least 0.3333 of this card's maximum. The lowest per-cell median anywhere in this repository's published corpus, 1275 MHz on a 1980 MHz part, sits 1.93x above that part's own floor; the 2026-09-11 fault sat 1.91x below its part's
        a FAIL    THE SESSION IS REFUSED AND THE POD IS RETURNED. A card that cannot hold a clock produces a ruler whose compute peak has collapsed while its memory side has not, and every roof fraction, ridge and alpha measured against that ruler is wrong rather than merely low.

  P2  and it is still holding it at the end of the window, not on the way down
        predicts  the last third of the window agrees with the first third within 0.05 of it, the same fraction `timing.clock_flags` applies to a cell, after the first 30 s have been discarded as the governor's ramp
        a FAIL    the card was still collapsing when the probe stopped. The median may be above the floor and the ceilings still unmeasurable, because the calibration that follows takes minutes and this window took two.

